From a674a666cd6a399793a3710c9bbac7ed384ac4f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:43:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Gate drain daemon exemption on no message ingress
 and bind root observer

Bounded no-ingress gate replaces unbounded ingress queue custody: require the running gateway effective config and primary/secondary adapter lists to be empty, retain a sealed inventory receipt, revalidate config inputs, revoke before any adapter construction. Cold capability alone cannot prove idle.

The fixed root observer binds boot/IID/epoch/latch generation/attempt before and after its scan, reads activated-account local results and never exempts arbitrary in-process callers. Document image-authored manifest and installed observer/producer integration.

Proof: canonical focused 41 tests green; 10 behavior mutants killed with clean baseline using sdlc-review mutants.py. Earlier drain/local-work/review/cron consumer selection green; final combined selection and remote exact-head review/CI remain before landing. No production baseline or idle ZERO claimed.
